---
import InfoLayout from "../../layouts/InfoLayout.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_NAME } from "../../lib/site";

const sections = [
  { slug: "agreement", text: "The agreement" },
  { slug: "accounts", text: "Accounts" },
  { slug: "your-content", text: "What you post" },
  { slug: "conduct", text: "How to behave" },
  { slug: "tools", text: "Tools" },
  { slug: "games", text: "Games" },
  { slug: "site-content", text: "The site’s own content" },
  { slug: "availability", text: "Availability and changes" },
  { slug: "disclaimers", text: "No guarantees" },
  { slug: "ending", text: "Ending" },
  { slug: "law", text: "Law and disputes" },
] as const;
---

<InfoLayout path="/legal/terms/" sections={sections} history>
  <h2 id="agreement">The agreement</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are between you and Trilleo (“I”, “me”), the individual who runs{" "}
    {SITE_NAME} at www.trilleo.net (“the site”). By using the site you agree to
    them, along with the <a href="/legal/privacy/">privacy policy</a>, the{" "}
    <a href="/legal/guidelines/">community guidelines</a> and the{" "}
    <a href="/legal/copyright/">copyright policy</a>. If you don’t agree, please
    don’t use the site. The site is free, and is offered as a personal,
    non-commercial project.
  </p>

  <h2 id="accounts">Accounts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You sign in with GitHub, so you also need to follow GitHub’s terms. Your
      account here belongs to you and no one else; keep your GitHub account
      secure, because whoever controls it controls this one.
    </li>
    <li>
      You must be at least 14 years old to make an account. Without one you can
      still read, use the tools and play.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can delete your account at any time from your account page. That
      deletes what you made here, as the privacy policy describes.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="your-content">What you post</h2>
  <p>
    Comments, your profile, uploaded files and anything else you add stay yours.
    So that the site can show them, you give me a worldwide, free, non-exclusive
    licence to store, copy, display and distribute them on the site (and in its
    feeds, backups and share images), and to make the technical changes that
    needs, such as thumbnails. The licence ends when you delete the content,
    except for copies already in backups (until they expire) and where someone
    else has quoted it in a reply.
  </p>
  <p>
    You are responsible for what you post, and you promise you have the right to
    post it. Files you publish may be downloaded by anyone; choose who can see a
    file when you upload it. Your first comment, and your uploads until you are
    trusted, are reviewed before they appear, as the community guidelines
    describe. Uploading isn’t open to every account yet.
  </p>

  <h2 id="conduct">How to behave</h2>
  <p>
    Follow the <a href="/legal/guidelines/">community guidelines</a>. In
    particular, don’t:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      break the law of mainland China, where the site is hosted, or of the place
      you are in;
    </li>
    <li>
      upload malware, or try to break into, overload or get around the limits of
      the site or its accounts (security research within the{" "}
      <a href="/security/">security policy</a> is welcome);
    </li>
    <li>
      scrape the site in a way that slows it down, or use automated accounts;
    </li>
    <li>
      pretend to be someone else, or use the site to send spam or advertising.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="tools">Tools</h2>
  <p>
    The tools are given as they are. File tools run in your browser and never
    upload your files; check their results before relying on them, and keep your
    own copies of anything important. Data saved in your browser can be lost if
    you clear it; data saved to your account is backed up, but is not a
    substitute for your own backups.
  </p>

  <h2 id="games">Games</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Coins, items, islands and everything else in the games are part of the
      game. They have no money value, can’t be exchanged for money, and aren’t
      your property. Don’t buy, sell or trade them for anything outside the
      game.
    </li>
    <li>The Bazaar is a market between players for in-game items only.</li>
    <li>
      Play fair: no bots, scripts, or exploiting bugs. If you find a bug, report
      it. The server checks every action; progress gained by breaking the rules
      can be rolled back, and leaderboard places removed.
    </li>
    <li>
      Games may be rebalanced, changed or, rarely, reset, and may end. You’ll be
      told before a reset.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="site-content">The site’s own content</h2>
  <p>
    The writing, design, images, pictograms and games on the site are © Trilleo
    unless stated otherwise. You may quote and link to them with credit. Source
    code is open where its repository on GitHub says so, under the licence
    stated there. Fonts and libraries belong to their makers; see the{" "}
    <a href="/colophon/">colophon</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some content is about Minecraft. {SITE_NAME} is not an official Minecraft
    product, and is not approved by or associated with Mojang or Microsoft.
    Minecraft is a trademark of Mojang Synergies AB.
  </p>

  <h2 id="availability">Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>
    The site is run by one person in their own time. It may be unavailable,
    change, lose features or close. If it closes, I will give at least 30 days’
    notice when I can, so you can download your data. These terms may change;
    the date at the top shows when they last did, and changes that affect your
    rights are announced before they apply. Using the site after that means you
    accept the new terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="disclaimers">No guarantees</h2>
  <p>
    The site, its tools and games are provided “as is”, without warranties of
    any kind. To the extent the law allows, I am not liable for indirect or
    consequential losses, lost data or lost profits from using the site, and my
    total liability is limited to 100 yuan. Nothing in these terms limits
    liability that the law doesn’t allow to be limited, or your rights as a
    consumer where you live.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ending">Ending</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using the site and delete your account at any time. I may hide
    content, limit features, or suspend or block an account that breaks these
    terms or the guidelines, usually with a warning first and always with a way
    to appeal (see the guidelines). Parts of these terms that by their nature
    should last (such as the licence for content already quoted, and the limits
    of liability) survive the end of your account.
  </p>

  <h2 id="law">Law and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the People’s Republic of China
    (excluding Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan). Please{" "}
    <a href="/contact/">write to me</a> first, at{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>; most things can be
    sorted out that way. Otherwise, disputes go to the people’s court with
    jurisdiction where I live, unless the law where you live gives you the right
    to bring them there.
  </p>
</InfoLayout>
